==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Oni Landshaker Kozuchimaru''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Issun Boshi has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Issun Boshi is most comparable to cheap rusher units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], that are able to quickly deal damage against enemies even when they're vulnerable for only a few seconds. While their base damage is too low for use against enemies outside of their targeted traits, with Massive Damage they're decent against Traitless and Angel enemies, with their damage being slightly lower than a similarly-leveled Bullet Train Cat.

Issun Boshi's high knockback count is a double-edged sword. On one hand, combined with their low range and health, it can be difficult to land hits as enemies are able to easily juggle and kill them; made worse by their small but noticeable foreswing which requires more precise timing than other rushers. However, on the other hand, with weaken support from the likes of [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] or [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] they are able to take advantage of any hits they survive through rebounds and land multiple hits back, significantly improving the potential damage they can dish out. Their Surge Immunity is a nice bonus by preventing them from being walled out by a long-lasting surge, but their low range can lead to them acting as a stepping stone for surges to land against any non-surge immune units.

Overall, Issun Boshi acts as a decent alternative to Bullet Train Cat against Traitless and Angel enemies, sacrificing the latter's consistency and ease of use with the potential for higher damage with proper support along with a shorter recharge time.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Oni Landshaker Kozuchimaru seems promising at first glance. Their health is decently high for a rebound rusher, which, combined with their many knockbacks, allows them to more easily land multiple hits onto enemies quickly; even better if the enemy is weakened. They also gain an Omni Strike that doubles their effective range, allowing them to more easily land hits onto specific targets as well as being able to damage a larger crowd. Along with their cooldown and cost being both low for an uber, they initially sounds like a great pick against both Traitless and Angel enemies.

However, they are massively held back by their laughably low damage even when considering the boost from Massive Damage. Not only does this make them a rather poor choice against other traits, but even against Traitless and Angel enemies, their damage is incredibly underwhelming even compared to other rusher units that don't target their traits such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]]. This also makes their low range a considerably larger weakness, as landing hits tends to be more struggle than what it rewards you.

In the end, in spite of their many unique traits for a rusher, Oni Landshaker Kozuchimaru is severely let down by their low attack stat by the mid to late game.

==='''True Form'''===
Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru gains a huge 50% damage boost, fixing their main weakness and helping make them a significantly better rusher. With their vastly improved damage, Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru is able to better take advantage of the strengths they had in their evolved form. Their Omni Strike allows them to deal with large crowds of enemies and ensure that peons in front of their target don't block their attack. Their decently high health combined with their multiple knockbacks allows them to dish out large amounts of damage quickly by taking advantage of their rebound allowing them to land numerous hits swiftly, allowing them to deal large chunks of damage to threats such as [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]], [[St. Dober]], and [[Kappy Jr.]] in just a few seconds. In the latter 2 cases, their surge immunity also ensures they won't get juggled around by their surges. Aside from that, their freeze immunity allows them to better counter [[Henry]] as they no longer have to worry about getting frozen by the anglerfish. It should be noted that this True Form does not address its issues with low range or noticeable foreswing, which could still lead to difficulties landing hits onto certain enemies. However, their improved speed does make timing easier, and the attack boost makes landing any hits considerably more rewarding.

Overall, the simple yet effective boosts Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru gains makes them go from an underwhelming rusher to a superb anti-Traitless and Angel nuker who can deal with large crowds or annoying threats swiftly.

{{Job|Classification = Rusher & Nuker}}

